/-!
# The subsheaf of an invertible module generated by finitely many sections, on a regular curve

Let `X` be an integral regular scheme of dimension at most one, `L` an invertible `𝒪_X`-module
and `s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)` a finite family of global sections, not all zero. Then the subsheaf of `L`
generated by the family is again invertible.

This is [Stacks, Tag 0CC4] in the shape its consumers use, and it is the second half of the proof
of [Stacks, Tag 0CCP]: a basis of a linear series need not generate `L`, but the subsheaf
`L' ⊆ L` it does generate is invertible, so [Stacks, Tag 01NE] applies to `L'`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules.isTorsionFree_of_isInvertibleModule`: an invertible
  module on an integral locally Noetherian scheme is torsion free.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules.Γgerm_genericPoint_ne_zero_of_ne_zero`: a nonzero
  global section of an invertible module on an integral scheme has nonzero germ at the generic
  point.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules.finrank_stalk_genericPoint_eq_one_of_isInvertible`:
  the stalk of an invertible module at the generic point of an integral scheme is one dimensional
  over the function field.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules.fiberRank_genericPoint_spanRestrictModule_eq_one`:
  the subsheaf generated by the family has fibre rank one at the generic point.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules.isInvertibleModule_spanRestrictModule`: **the
  subsheaf generated by the family is invertible.**

## Implementation notes

The chain is the one [Stacks, Tag 0CC4] is stated for, plus the rank bookkeeping that turns
"finite locally free" into "invertible":

* the subsheaf is quasi-coherent and of finite type, hence coherent on a locally Noetherian
  scheme, `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PFAffineSubsheaf.isCoherent_spanRestrictModule`;
* it is torsion free, being a submodule of the invertible — hence reflexive, hence torsion free —
  module `L`, by `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules.isTorsionFree_toSheafOfModules`;
* so it is finite locally free by Tag 0CC4,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.isTorsionFree_iff_isFiniteLocallyFree`;
* its rank is *one* because the rank of a finite locally free module on an integral scheme is the
  fibre rank at any single point,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_of_fiberRank_eq`, and at the
  generic point the subsheaf is a nonzero subspace of the one-dimensional function-field vector
  space `L_η`;
* and finite locally free of rank one is invertible, [Stacks, Tag 0B8M],
  `Stacks.InvertibleRankOneScheme.isInvertibleModule_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one`.

**Why a nonvanishing hypothesis is unavoidable.** If every `s i` is zero then the subsheaf is the
zero module, which is finite locally free of rank *zero* and not invertible. So the hypothesis
`hi` is not a convenience: the statement is false without it.

**Two spellings of invertibility.** `Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf _ L`, while
`AlgebraicGeometry.isReflexive_of_isInvertible` is stated for
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj _ L`. Instance search does not cross
between them, so `AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleSheafGeneral.isInvertible_of_isInvertibleModule` is
supplied by hand. Quasi-coherence and finite type of an invertible module are not reproved here:
they are `Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.isQuasicoherent_of_isInvertibleModule` and
`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.isFiniteType_of_isInvertibleModule`, both already at the
`Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule` spelling.

The map on stalks is `Stacks.ModuleStalk.mapFun`, upgraded here to a `LinearMap` over the stalk
of the structure sheaf so that `LinearMap.finrank_le_finrank_of_injective` applies; its
injectivity is `TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor_map_injective_of_app_injective` fed by injectivity
of the inclusion on sections.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CC4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CC4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CCP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CCP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01C9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01C9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AY2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AY2)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PFAffineSubsheaf
open Stacks.ModuleStalk

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### Consequences of invertibility, at the `Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule` spelling -/

/-- **An invertible module on an integral locally Noetherian scheme is torsion free**: it is
reflexive, and a reflexive module is torsion free, [Stacks, Tag 0AY2]. -/
theorem isTorsionFree_of_isInvertibleModule [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (L : X.Modules) [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] : IsTorsionFree L :=
  have := AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleSheafGeneral.isInvertible_of_isInvertibleModule L
  isTorsionFree_of_isReflexive L (AlgebraicGeometry.isReflexive_of_isInvertible X L)

/-- **A nonzero global section of an invertible module on an integral scheme has nonzero germ at
the generic point.** The germ map at the generic point is injective on the sections of a
torsion-free quasi-coherent module,
`AlgebraicGeometry.injective_generic_germ_of_isTorsionFree`. -/
theorem Γgerm_genericPoint_ne_zero_of_ne_zero [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (L : X.Modules) [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] {t : Γ(L, ⊤)} (ht : t ≠ 0) :
    (L.presheaf.Γgerm (genericPoint X)).hom t ≠ 0 := by
  let := Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.isQuasicoherent_of_isInvertibleModule L
  intro h0
  refine ht (AlgebraicGeometry.injective_generic_germ_of_isTorsionFree L
    (isTorsionFree_of_isInvertibleModule L) (U := ⊤) True.intro ?_)
  rw [map_zero]
  exact h0

/-- **The stalk of an invertible module at the generic point of an integral scheme is one
dimensional.** An invertible module is finite locally free of rank one, [Stacks, Tag 0B8M], so
its fibre rank is one everywhere, [Stacks, Tag 01C9]; at the generic point of an integral scheme
the fibre rank is the dimension of the stalk over the function field. -/
theorem finrank_stalk_genericPoint_eq_one_of_isInvertible [IsIntegral X] (L : X.Modules)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] :
    Module.finrank (X.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X))
      (L.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) = 1 := by
  let := Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.isFiniteType_of_isInvertibleModule L
  let := Stacks.InvertibleRankOneScheme.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isInvertibleModule X L
  rw [← Scheme.Modules.fiberRank_genericPoint_eq_finrank_stalk L]
  exact Scheme.Modules.fiberRank_eq_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank L 1 _

/-! ### The subsheaf generated by a finite family of sections -/

section Span

variable [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (L : X.Modules)
  [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] {ι : Type*}

attribute [local instance]
  Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.isQuasicoherent_of_isInvertibleModule

/-- The map on stalks induced by the inclusion of the subsheaf generated by a family, as a linear
map over the stalk of the structure sheaf. -/
def stalkMapSpanRestrict (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) (x : X) :
    (spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)).presheaf.stalk x →ₗ[X.presheaf.stalk x]
      L.presheaf.stalk x where
  toFun := mapFun (spanRestrictSubsheafι L (Set.range s)) x
  map_add' := mapFun_add (spanRestrictSubsheafι L (Set.range s)) x
  map_smul' := mapFun_smul (spanRestrictSubsheafι L (Set.range s)) x

omit [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] in
/-- **The map on stalks induced by the inclusion of the subsheaf generated by a family is
injective**, the inclusion being injective on sections over every open. -/
theorem injective_stalkMapSpanRestrict (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) (x : X) :
    Function.Injective (stalkMapSpanRestrict L s x) :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor_map_injective_of_app_injective
    (f := (spanRestrictSubsheafι L (Set.range s)).mapPresheaf)
    (fun U => injective_app_spanRestrictSubsheafι L (Set.range s) U) x

/-- **The subsheaf generated by the family has fibre rank one at the generic point.** It injects
into the one-dimensional function-field vector space `L_η`, so its dimension there is at most
one; it is nonzero because the germ of `s i` at `η` is, so the dimension is exactly one. -/
theorem fiberRank_genericPoint_spanRestrictModule_eq_one (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤))
    (hfin : (Set.range s).Finite) {i : ι}
    (hi : (L.presheaf.Γgerm (genericPoint X)).hom (s i) ≠ 0) :
    (spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)).fiberRank (genericPoint X) = 1 := by
  let : Field (X.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) := inferInstanceAs (Field X.functionField)
  let := Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.isFiniteType_of_isInvertibleModule L
  have hcoh : _root_.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent (spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)) :=
    isCoherent_spanRestrictModule L hfin
  let : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u} (spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)) :=
    _root_.IsCoherent.toIsFiniteType _
  have hfinL : Module.Finite (X.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X))
      (L.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) :=
    Stacks.StalkFiniteType.finite_stalk L _
  have hfinL' : Module.Finite (X.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X))
      ((spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)).presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) :=
    Stacks.StalkFiniteType.finite_stalk _ _
  -- The germ of `spanRangeSection L s i` at `η` is nonzero, so the stalk is nontrivial.
  have hne : ((spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)).presheaf.Γgerm (genericPoint X)).hom
      (spanRangeSection L s i) ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    have hmap := mapFun_Γgerm (spanRestrictSubsheafι L (Set.range s)) (genericPoint X)
      (spanRangeSection L s i)
    rw [app_spanRestrictSubsheafι_spanRangeSection] at hmap
    have hbundled : ∀ y : (spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)).presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X),
        mapFun (spanRestrictSubsheafι L (Set.range s)) (genericPoint X) y =
          stalkMapSpanRestrict L s (genericPoint X) y := fun _ => rfl
    refine hi (hmap.symm.trans ?_)
    rw [hbundled, h0, map_zero]
  have hnt :
      Nontrivial ((spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)).presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) :=
    nontrivial_of_ne _ _ hne
  have hle : Module.finrank (X.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X))
      ((spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)).presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) ≤ 1 :=
    le_trans (LinearMap.finrank_le_finrank_of_injective
        (injective_stalkMapSpanRestrict L s (genericPoint X)))
      (finrank_stalk_genericPoint_eq_one_of_isInvertible L).le
  have hpos : 0 < Module.finrank (X.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X))
      ((spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)).presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) :=
    Module.finrank_pos_iff.mpr hnt
  rw [Scheme.Modules.fiberRank_genericPoint_eq_finrank_stalk]
  omega

/-- **The subsheaf of an invertible module generated by a finite family of global sections, one of
which does not vanish at the generic point, is invertible.** This is [Stacks, Tag 0CC4] in the
shape the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0CCP] uses it. -/
theorem isInvertibleModule_spanRestrictModule (hreg : IsRegular X)
    (hdim : topologicalKrullDim X ≤ 1) (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) (hfin : (Set.range s).Finite) {i : ι}
    (hi : (L.presheaf.Γgerm (genericPoint X)).hom (s i) ≠ 0) :
    Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X (spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)) := by
  have hcoh : _root_.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent (spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)) :=
    isCoherent_spanRestrictModule L hfin
  have htf : IsTorsionFree (spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)) :=
    isTorsionFree_toSheafOfModules (isTorsionFree_of_isInvertibleModule L)
      (spanRestrictSubsheaf L (Set.range s))
  have hflf : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u}
      (R := X.ringCatSheaf) (spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)) :=
    (AlgebraicGeometry.isTorsionFree_iff_isFiniteLocallyFree hreg hdim _).mp htf
  have := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_of_fiberRank_eq
    (spanRestrictModule L (Set.range s)) 1 (genericPoint X)
    (fiberRank_genericPoint_spanRestrictModule_eq_one L s hfin hi)
  exact Stacks.InvertibleRankOneScheme.isInvertibleModule_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one X _

end Span

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules

end
